# Project memory merge strategy (autocommit-hook effort, ticket 05).
#
# Two branches that each APPEND §-delimited entries to MEMORY.md would conflict
# at the same insertion point on every forward-merge. This scoped attribute
# routes the file through the `pi-memory` §-union merge driver, which splits on
# §, unions entries by trimmed content (dedup), and rejoins — so both branches'
# new entries survive and common base entries aren't duplicated.
#
# The driver COMMAND lives in per-clone git config (merge.pi-memory.driver) — it
# is NOT committed, because the script path varies per install. The
# hermes-memory autocommit hook self-configures it idempotently on first commit
# when a repo opts in (config.json → autoCommitProjectMemory). Until then git
# falls back to a normal merge for this file (neutral — no worse than without it).
MEMORY.md merge=pi-memory
